    "what to release": "The giving that comes from guilt rather than abundance. That kind of giving exhausts the giver and subtly diminishes the receiver.",
    "the seed": "Plant the intention to create one genuinely balanced exchange in your life — something that nourishes both parties.",
    "the obstacle": "The discomfort of equal footing. Many people are more comfortable in the role of giver or receiver than in real mutuality.",
    "first steps": "Identify whether you are currently playing one role exclusively. Take one step toward balance.",
    "what has grown": "Generosity — the real kind, rooted in enough, freely given, without strings.",
    "what is illuminated": "The power dynamics in your giving and receiving. The full moon shows who holds the scales and whether they are balanced.",
    "what hides in the light": "The conditions attached to the gift. Even generous people sometimes give in ways that bind.",
    "what must be released": "Charity that comes from a need to feel superior, or dependency that comes from a need to feel cared for.",
    "how to let go": "Give without tracking the return. Or: ask for what you need without apologizing for the need.",
